   "tools_usd": 0.0,
   "comments": [],
   "parsed": true,
   "raw": "{\"decision\":\"escalate\",\"evidence\":[\"F1\"],\"comments\":[]}\n```\n\nI could not establish that this is safe to ship from the diff alone. Static checks are clean and the suite at head passes (347 passed), but the main risks are outside what those cover.\n\n- **Unverified CLI flags:** `main.py` builds a `pagedserve.cli serve` command with flags I cannot confirm exist: `--enable-prefix-caching`, `--served-model-name`, `--quantization`, `--tensor-parallel-size` and `--enable-cuda-graphs`. The test only checks the string list. A wrong flag would make the server exit at startup on every worker.\n- **Removed tests:** F1 reports 2 tests removed. They covered the old engine-based handler, which this change replaces, so removal is plausible. I cannot confirm they were not covering behaviour that still matters.\n- **Untested paths:** The following cannot be exercised in CI, which uses an ASGI transport rather than a real server process.\n  - `wait_for_server`\n  - the real subprocess startup\n  - the Runpod SDK integration\n  - the `return_aggregate_stream` behaviour with string SSE chunks\n- **Dropped behaviour:** the old handler's `piecewise` and `chunked` defaults are no longer set in the worker. The new code relies on CLI defaults I have not seen.\n\nA human should check the CLI flag names against `pagedserve/cli.py` and run one real worker startup."
  },
